    {
      "id": 38,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        2350,
        90
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        900
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 37,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3 All-in-One\n\n### Switching modes\nOnly the **SaveVideo** nodes decide what runs. ComfyUI executes backwards from active outputs, so the muted branch costs nothing and is never validated.\n\n- **Mode A (FL2VA)** - unmute `MODE A OUTPUT`, mute `MODE B OUTPUT` (Ctrl+M)\n- **Mode B (Ref2VA)** - the reverse\n\n### Reference video / audio (Mode B)\nThree extra loaders are wired into the reference node and shipped **muted**. Optional inputs, so muted feeders are simply dropped from the prompt - nothing errors.\n- `Reference Video` -> Split -> feeds `ref_video_0` (frames) and `ref_video_audio_0` (its soundtrack). Unmute **both** the loader and the splitter.\n- `Reference Audio` -> feeds `ref_audio_0`. Voice, music or ambience to drive the generated track.\nCall them in the prompt as `<Video 1>` and `<Audio 1>`.\n\n**Also swap the checkpoint** in UNETLoader to match:\n- Mode A -> `minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot`\n- Mode B -> `minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot`\n\n### LoRA\nBoth loaders are bypassed. Select a file, then Ctrl+B to enable. Chain order is LoRA -> Sigma Shift -> Spectrum, which is what Spectrum requires.\n\n### Spectrum\nNeeds `ComfyUI-Spectrum-MiniMax-H3` in custom_nodes. Values shown are the conservative preset. Aggressive is blend_weight 0.75 / flex_window 3.0.\nSet `enabled` to false to A/B against the native path - it returns the model untouched, nothing else changes.\n`res_multistep` keeps its final three solver steps native regardless of tail_actual_steps.\n\n### Do not launch with --use-sage-attention\nSage produces pure noise on H3. Spectrum is the accelerator to use instead - different mechanism, it skips transformer evaluations rather than changing the attention kernel."
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
